# rc.6 Node/Chrome numerical discrepancy investigation

The extra cross-runtime whole-envelope equality assertion was invalid for these exact runtime builds. No product regression was found: the root production Caracas receipt is exactly equal to the author's earlier real Chrome receipt. Fresh real Chrome calculations produce exactly the same rc.5 and rc.6 numbers for all 16 historical inputs. No product or numerical tolerance was changed.

## What was proved

The unchanged author subject bundle is 238,053 bytes, SHA256 `19f4c6c1b2315527602cf33bb33338be0f2ec639a08492ba8d411b2c77d2df5d`. Its retained build identity includes the actual rc.5 and rc.6 module graphs and frozen receipt helper. The prior package verification is retained. A fresh check also proves all 23 installed root rc.6 members equal the immutable archive SHA256 `09c3e63432f8ba2e9df05af137c42f65ab039740a207a89418d9e6470ea3db3e`.

- Root's actual downloaded Caracas envelope equals the prior author Chrome envelope exactly, including all receipt context and numerical fields. This compares the production build with the separate unminified author bundle.
- All 16 fresh historical Chrome results equal prior author Chrome results exactly. Both Node versions likewise reproduce their original 16 reports exactly.
- rc.5 and rc.6 public natal output has exact numerical equality at every identical explicit input in each of Node 22, Node 24 and Chrome, excluding only the intentionally different engineVersion. Both Nodes' trace and chart values also match one another exactly.
- The actual installed unbundled rc.6 public package equals the immutable bundled rc.6 result for all 16 inputs on both Nodes. Package/build path differences therefore do not explain this counterexample.

## Causal control

For synthetic Caracas input UTC `1890-01-01T04:27:44.000Z`, latitude -3.1, longitude -60.02, requested Placidus, known time, flags dst-gap/lmt, fresh isolated module instances record 270,141 Math calls. Wrapping Math leaves each native chart unchanged. The first divergence is at zero-based call 17:

`Math.cos(-81.09991224236799)` gives `0.8356414579161423` in both Nodes and `0.8356414579161422` in Chrome. Direct isolated calls outside the chart reproduce this difference. There are 7,817 same-argument/different-result observations (4,404 cos, 3,404 sin and 9 atan2) in the corresponding fresh traces.

Replaying the exact Node Math results in a fresh Chrome module reproduces the entire Node chart exactly. A stronger separate replay substitutes only cos, sin and atan2 results; every other Math function executes natively in Chrome. Every operation name, every argument and every remaining native result matches exactly for all 270,141 calls, and the entire resulting chart matches Node exactly. This is a controlled causal explanation, not an inference from the differences being small.

The actual source also explains sensitivity of the lunar node path: Astronomy Engine GeoMoonState estimates velocity from positions separated by ±0.00001 day; the SDK computes instantaneous angular momentum and a node longitude, then estimates node speed at ±0.25 day. The trace establishes the concrete runtime cause. This source observation does not certify a general numerical error bound.

## Observed extent and limits

The original Caracas discrepancy has node longitude/degree delta `1.1963265933445655e-9` degrees and speed delta `2.2773747332394123e-9` degrees/day; ordinary affected leaf deltas are `5.684341886080802e-14`. Across the 16 retained historical cases there are 110 differing numeric leaves. Maximum observed longitude delta is `3.981028839916689e-9` degrees (North Node, Port-au-Prince); maximum observed speed and any numeric leaf delta is `1.8382138478045817e-8` degrees/day (North Node, Colombo). These are measured values, not new acceptance thresholds, a universal bound, or an astronomical accuracy certification.

Exact runtimes are Node 22.23.2 / V8 12.4.254.21-node.56, Node 24.19.0 / V8 13.6.233.17-node.51, and actual Chrome 152.0.7977.83 / V8 15.2.124.21. ECMAScript explicitly permits implementation-approximated results for the relevant transcendental functions; see the [official Math.cos section](https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/numbers-and-dates.html#sec-math.cos), [Math.sin](https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/numbers-and-dates.html#sec-math.sin), and [Math.atan2](https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/numbers-and-dates.html#sec-math.atan2). No cross-runtime bit-equality guarantee is established or claimed. The precise V8 library implementation change was not investigated and is not needed for the experimentally proven explanation.

This is the author agent's bounded diagnostic verification, not a new independent numerical oracle, independent human signoff or a replacement for existing numerical acceptance tests. Root owns integration and release decisions. The original failing assertion and all intermediate harness failures remain intact. No product source, test tolerance, SDK archive, shared resolver policy or active lifecycle was changed.

## Evidence and cleanup

RESULTS.json is the readable assertion-backed comparison. Full exact traces, scripts, original failures, manifests, copied numerical source, served-byte identities and browser screenshot are preserved losslessly in raw-evidence.tar.gz. raw-member-manifest.json records each original uncompressed member size/SHA256; the archive was decompressed and every member verified. COMMANDS.md records invocations and the corrected harness failures. All browser contexts, Chrome processes and owned servers are closed. Final calculation ran offline, with no external requests and no browser errors.
